{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":62522,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"b5b16c71-40f4-5c36-9ba1-d209296d2c8b","total_cost_usd":0.5045459999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9940,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6029,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9940,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6029,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9940,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9940},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4181,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004275999999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":6029,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":9940,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.50027,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-e2-reviewer-fable-26\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:102f7842bc112abba84f\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The declared independent-unit column is vessel_id, and the data description states each vessel appears exactly once with a single harvest measurement.\",\"observed_value\":\"vessel_id declared as independent unit; each vessel measured once\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":20,\"end_line\":21,\"quoted_text\":\"One row is: one pilot fermenter, described by the single ethanol titer measured in its harvest sample\\nIndependent unit column: vessel_id\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":8,\"end_line\":9,\"quoted_text\":\"table. No vessel was reused, split between strains, or sampled a second time, so the\\ntwelve rows stand for twelve separate experimental runs.\"}]},{\"description\":\"data/input.csv contains exactly twelve data rows with twelve distinct vessel_id values V01 through V12; no vessel_id repeats, and each arm has six vessels.\",\"observed_value\":\"12 rows, 12 unique vessel_id values (V01–V12), 6 wildtype + 6 engineered\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":13,\"quoted_text\":\"vessel_id,strain_arm,inoculum_lot,final_titer_g_per_l\\nV01,wildtype,LOT-A1,41.2\\nV02,engineered,LOT-B1,48.3\\nV03,wildtype,LOT-A2,43.8\\nV04,engineered,LOT-B2,51.0\\nV05,wildtype,LOT-A3,39.6\\nV06,engineered,LOT-B3,46.9\\nV07,wildtype,LOT-A4,44.5\\nV08,engineered,LOT-B4,49.6\\nV09,wildtype,LOT-A5,42.1\\nV10,engineered,LOT-B5,52.2\\nV11,wildtype,LOT-A6,40.8\\nV12,engineered,LOT-B6,47.5\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow explicitly guards against repeated independent-unit entries: read_vessels raises a ValueError if any vessel_id appears more than once, so duplicated units could not silently enter the test.\",\"observed_value\":\"duplicate vessel_id triggers ValueError\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":21,\"end_line\":31,\"quoted_text\":\"def read_vessels(path):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return the CSV rows, refusing any vessel that shows up twice.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    with path.open(\\\"r\\\", encoding=\\\"ascii\\\", newline=\\\"\\\") as handle:\\n        rows = list(csv.DictReader(handle))\\n    seen = set()\\n    for row in rows:\\n        vessel = row[\\\"vessel_id\\\"]\\n        if vessel in seen:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"vessel_id appears more than once: \\\" + vessel)\\n        seen.add(vessel)\\n    return rows\"}]},{\"description\":\"The selected result's reported statistics are reproducible from one titer per vessel: complete separation of arms (wildtype max 44.5 < engineered min 46.9) gives U = 6*6 = 36 and exact two-sided p = 2/C(12,6) = 2/924 ≈ 0.00216, and arm means 42.00 vs 49.25 g/L give the reported +7.25 g/L gap, confirming the test was run on the 12 vessel-level rows with no unit entering twice.\",\"observed_value\":{\"U\":36,\"p_exact_two_sided\":0.002164502,\"mean_wildtype\":42,\"mean_engineered\":49.25,\"mean_gap\":7.25},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":21,\"end_line\":24,\"quoted_text\":\"The engineered vessels occupy the six highest ranks,\\ngiving U = 36.0 with an exact two-sided p-value of 0.00216. The rank-biserial\\ncorrelation is 1.000, the Hodges-Lehmann shift estimate is 7.25 g/L, and the gap\\nbetween arm means is 7.25 g/L.\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":26,\"end_line\":26,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Exact two-sided Mann-Whitney U test on 12 independent pilot fermenters (6 engineered vs 6 wild-type, one harvest titer per vessel): U = 36.0, p = 0.00216, Hodges-Lehmann shift +7.25 g/L, so the engineered strain reaches the higher final titer.\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The analysis does feed all rows into a row-independent procedure (an exact Mann-Whitney U test via scipy.stats.mannwhitneyu), which is the kind of procedure the issue class targets; however, since every vessel_id contributes exactly one row, the precondition of repeated independent-unit entry is absent.\",\"observed_value\":\"row-independent test present, but no repeated units enter it\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":57,\"end_line\":58,\"quoted_text\":\"outcome = stats.mannwhitneyu(engineered, wild, alternative=\\\"two-sided\\\",\\n                                 method=\\\"exact\\\")\"}]},{\"description\":\"inoculum_lot is a second identifier that could in principle group vessels and induce dependence between rows, but the description states every vessel had its own lot, and the CSV shows twelve distinct lot values (LOT-A1..A6, LOT-B1..B6), so no lot repeats across vessels.\",\"observed_value\":\"12 distinct inoculum_lot values, one per vessel\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":16,\"end_line\":17,\"quoted_text\":\"- inoculum_lot: identifier of the seed culture lot used for that vessel; every vessel\\n  had a lot of its own.\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":2,\"end_line\":13,\"quoted_text\":\"V01,wildtype,LOT-A1,41.2\\nV02,engineered,LOT-B1,48.3\\nV03,wildtype,LOT-A2,43.8\\nV04,engineered,LOT-B2,51.0\\nV05,wildtype,LOT-A3,39.6\\nV06,engineered,LOT-B3,46.9\\nV07,wildtype,LOT-A4,44.5\\nV08,engineered,LOT-B4,49.6\\nV09,wildtype,LOT-A5,42.1\\nV10,engineered,LOT-B5,52.2\\nV11,wildtype,LOT-A6,40.8\\nV12,engineered,LOT-B6,47.5\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I tried to falsify the no-issue verdict by (1) scanning every vessel_id in data/input.csv for repeats — all twelve values V01–V12 are distinct, matching the declared independent-unit column; (2) checking whether the workflow could multiply rows before testing — arm_titers only filters rows by strain_arm and read_vessels rejects duplicates, so no row duplication or expansion occurs upstream of stats.mannwhitneyu; (3) checking whether any other column (inoculum_lot) encodes a repeated unit disguised under distinct vessel_ids — all twelve lot values are unique, and the description states one lot per vessel; and (4) recomputing the reported statistics from the raw data (means 42.00 vs 49.25, complete separation giving U = 36 and exact p = 2/924 ≈ 0.00216), which matches the report exactly and is consistent with exactly one entry per vessel. None of these attempts produced evidence of a repeated independent-unit entry into the row-independent test.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-e2-reviewer-fable-26","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:102f7842bc112abba84f","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The declared independent-unit column is vessel_id, and the data description states each vessel appears exactly once with a single harvest measurement.","observed_value":"vessel_id declared as independent unit; each vessel measured once","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":20,"end_line":21,"quoted_text":"One row is: one pilot fermenter, described by the single ethanol titer measured in its harvest sample\nIndependent unit column: vessel_id"},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":8,"end_line":9,"quoted_text":"table. No vessel was reused, split between strains, or sampled a second time, so the\ntwelve rows stand for twelve separate experimental runs."}]},{"description":"data/input.csv contains exactly twelve data rows with twelve distinct vessel_id values V01 through V12; no vessel_id repeats, and each arm has six vessels.","observed_value":"12 rows, 12 unique vessel_id values (V01–V12), 6 wildtype + 6 engineered","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":1,"end_line":13,"quoted_text":"vessel_id,strain_arm,inoculum_lot,final_titer_g_per_l\nV01,wildtype,LOT-A1,41.2\nV02,engineered,LOT-B1,48.3\nV03,wildtype,LOT-A2,43.8\nV04,engineered,LOT-B2,51.0\nV05,wildtype,LOT-A3,39.6\nV06,engineered,LOT-B3,46.9\nV07,wildtype,LOT-A4,44.5\nV08,engineered,LOT-B4,49.6\nV09,wildtype,LOT-A5,42.1\nV10,engineered,LOT-B5,52.2\nV11,wildtype,LOT-A6,40.8\nV12,engineered,LOT-B6,47.5"}]},{"description":"The workflow explicitly guards against repeated independent-unit entries: read_vessels raises a ValueError if any vessel_id appears more than once, so duplicated units could not silently enter the test.","observed_value":"duplicate vessel_id triggers ValueError","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":21,"end_line":31,"quoted_text":"def read_vessels(path):\n    \"\"\"Return the CSV rows, refusing any vessel that shows up twice.\"\"\"\n    with path.open(\"r\", encoding=\"ascii\", newline=\"\") as handle:\n        rows = list(csv.DictReader(handle))\n    seen = set()\n    for row in rows:\n        vessel = row[\"vessel_id\"]\n        if vessel in seen:\n            raise ValueError(\"vessel_id appears more than once: \" + vessel)\n        seen.add(vessel)\n    return rows"}]},{"description":"The selected result's reported statistics are reproducible from one titer per vessel: complete separation of arms (wildtype max 44.5 < engineered min 46.9) gives U = 6*6 = 36 and exact two-sided p = 2/C(12,6) = 2/924 ≈ 0.00216, and arm means 42.00 vs 49.25 g/L give the reported +7.25 g/L gap, confirming the test was run on the 12 vessel-level rows with no unit entering twice.","observed_value":{"U":36,"p_exact_two_sided":0.002164502,"mean_wildtype":42,"mean_engineered":49.25,"mean_gap":7.25},"source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":21,"end_line":24,"quoted_text":"The engineered vessels occupy the six highest ranks,\ngiving U = 36.0 with an exact two-sided p-value of 0.00216. The rank-biserial\ncorrelation is 1.000, the Hodges-Lehmann shift estimate is 7.25 g/L, and the gap\nbetween arm means is 7.25 g/L."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":26,"end_line":26,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Exact two-sided Mann-Whitney U test on 12 independent pilot fermenters (6 engineered vs 6 wild-type, one harvest titer per vessel): U = 36.0, p = 0.00216, Hodges-Lehmann shift +7.25 g/L, so the engineered strain reaches the higher final titer."}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The analysis does feed all rows into a row-independent procedure (an exact Mann-Whitney U test via scipy.stats.mannwhitneyu), which is the kind of procedure the issue class targets; however, since every vessel_id contributes exactly one row, the precondition of repeated independent-unit entry is absent.","observed_value":"row-independent test present, but no repeated units enter it","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":57,"end_line":58,"quoted_text":"outcome = stats.mannwhitneyu(engineered, wild, alternative=\"two-sided\",\n                                 method=\"exact\")"}]},{"description":"inoculum_lot is a second identifier that could in principle group vessels and induce dependence between rows, but the description states every vessel had its own lot, and the CSV shows twelve distinct lot values (LOT-A1..A6, LOT-B1..B6), so no lot repeats across vessels.","observed_value":"12 distinct inoculum_lot values, one per vessel","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":16,"end_line":17,"quoted_text":"- inoculum_lot: identifier of the seed culture lot used for that vessel; every vessel\n  had a lot of its own."},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":13,"quoted_text":"V01,wildtype,LOT-A1,41.2\nV02,engineered,LOT-B1,48.3\nV03,wildtype,LOT-A2,43.8\nV04,engineered,LOT-B2,51.0\nV05,wildtype,LOT-A3,39.6\nV06,engineered,LOT-B3,46.9\nV07,wildtype,LOT-A4,44.5\nV08,engineered,LOT-B4,49.6\nV09,wildtype,LOT-A5,42.1\nV10,engineered,LOT-B5,52.2\nV11,wildtype,LOT-A6,40.8\nV12,engineered,LOT-B6,47.5"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I tried to falsify the no-issue verdict by (1) scanning every vessel_id in data/input.csv for repeats — all twelve values V01–V12 are distinct, matching the declared independent-unit column; (2) checking whether the workflow could multiply rows before testing — arm_titers only filters rows by strain_arm and read_vessels rejects duplicates, so no row duplication or expansion occurs upstream of stats.mannwhitneyu; (3) checking whether any other column (inoculum_lot) encodes a repeated unit disguised under distinct vessel_ids — all twelve lot values are unique, and the description states one lot per vessel; and (4) recomputing the reported statistics from the raw data (means 42.00 vs 49.25, complete separation giving U = 36 and exact p = 2/924 ≈ 0.00216), which matches the report exactly and is consistent with exactly one entry per vessel. None of these attempts produced evidence of a repeated independent-unit entry into the row-independent test.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":31054,"ttft_stream_ms":3397,"time_to_request_ms":10,"type":"result","duration_ms":62966,"uuid":"994fb864-5d49-48c3-84bd-54ab761145b1"}
